{"kind":"problem","subkind":"conjecture","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"conj-1","file":"","label":"con1","number":"1.1","section":"sec-1","order":1,"title":"Conjecture","body_md":"\\label{con1}\r\nLet $G$ and $H$ be two finite non-abelian groups such that $\\Gamma_G\\cong \\Gamma_H$. Then $|G|=|H|$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"conj","item":"conjecture","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","name":"Conjecture 1.1 of","cites_in_head":["AAM"],"labels":["con1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":40,"to":42},"hash":"sha256:ad9652689b8e502bd232c3e382ba11a5b7ef0c3ae04e2b9f1510e867391d5b61","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"thm-1","file":"","label":"thm1","number":"1.2","section":"sec-1","order":2,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{thm1} Let $G$ and $H$ be two finite non-abelian  nilpotent groups\r\nwith irregular non-commuting graphs such that $\\Gamma_G\\cong\\Gamma_H$. Then $|G|=|H|$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["thm1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"none","origin":"own","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":54,"to":56},"hash":"sha256:68715ab84aaefd6aa773c9879d763bdc3dc904582f457f10096fe30d3bea4f8b","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"lem-1","file":"","number":"2.1","section":"sec-2","order":3,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"Let $G$ and $H$ be two finite non-abelian groups. If $\\phi:\\Gamma_G\\rightarrow \\Gamma_H$ is a graph isomorphism and $g$\r\nis a non-central element of $G$, then the following hold:\r\n\\begin{enumerate}\r\n\\item $|G|-|Z(G)|=|H|-|Z(H)|$.\r\n\\item $|G|-|C_G(g)|=|H|-|C_H(\\phi(g))|$.\r\n\\item $|C_G(g)|-|Z(C_G(g))|=|H|-|Z(C_H(\\phi(g)))|$, where $C_G(g)$ is not abelian.\r\n\\item If $C_G(g)$ is not abelian, then $\\Gamma_{C_G(g)}\\cong \\Gamma_{C_H(\\phi(g))}$.\r\n\\item Suppose that $C_1=C_G(g_1)$ and $C_i=C_{C_{i-1}}(g_i)$ for $i\\geq 2$, where $g_1\\in G\\setminus Z(G)$ and $g_i\\in C_{i-1}\\setminus Z(C_{i-1})$.\r\nThen there exists $k\\in\\mathbb{N}$ such that $C_k$ is an $AC$-group.\r\n\\item $|G|=|H|$ if and only if $|C_G(g)|=|C_H(\\phi(g))|$ if and only if $|Z(G)|=|Z(H)|$.\r\n\\end{enumerate}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","parts":[{"marker":"1.","from":5147,"to":5179},{"marker":"2.","from":5179,"to":5221},{"marker":"3.","from":5221,"to":5305},{"marker":"4.","from":5305,"to":5391},{"marker":"5.","from":5391,"to":5611},{"marker":"6.","from":5611,"to":5701}],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"here","origin":"own","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":75,"to":87},"hash":"sha256:2feab969462f7d15ffe12edd6672909d0afe5b246adb1c7ed3349d71656a4850","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-3","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"proof","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"proof-1","file":"","section":"sec-2","order":4,"title":"Proof","body_md":"It is straightforward. To prove (5), note that if the centralizer $C_i$ is not an $AC$-group, then some proper centralizer in $C_i$ is not abelian\r\nguaranteeing  the existence of an element $g_{i+1}$. On the other hand, $G$ is finite so the series $C_1\u003eC_2\u003e\\cdots\u003eC_i\u003e\\cdots$ will  eventually terminate  in\r\nan $AC$-group.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proof","item":"proof","head":"environment","scope":"paper","proves":"lem-1","attach":3,"span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":88,"to":92},"hash":"sha256:fab836c0bb746a293d00de548f7b1f77ac605265b7b4e50e78531cbec2a4fd5e","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#proof-1","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"lemma","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"lem-2","file":"","label":"l1","number":"2.2","section":"sec-2","order":5,"title":"Lemma","body_md":"\\label{l1} Let $G$ be a finite non-abelian group and $H$ be a group such that\r\n$\\Gamma_G\\cong \\Gamma_H$.  Then the following hold:\r\n\\begin{enumerate}\r\n\\item  $|C_H(h)|$ divides $(|g^G| - 1) (|Z(G)| - |Z(H)|)$ for any $g\\in G\\setminus Z(G)$ and $h=\\phi(g)$, where $\\phi$ is any graph isomorphism\r\nfrom $\\Gamma_G$ to $\\Gamma_H$.  \\item If $|Z(G)|\\geq |Z(H)|$ and $G$ contains a\r\nnon-central element  $g$ such that ${|C_G(g)|}^2\\geq |G|\\cdot|Z(G)|$, then $|G|=|H|$.\r\n\\end{enumerate}","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"lem","item":"statement/lemma","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","name":"see e.g. Theorem 2.1 of","cites_in_head":["AADS"],"labels":["l1"],"parts":[{"marker":"1.","from":6281,"to":6458},{"marker":"2.","from":6458,"to":6594}],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"cited","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":93,"to":100},"hash":"sha256:cc0bda8611cc6f398a3a5e0520622b84d0e9018a2e3b60f952e4b3d21d8d035f","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-4","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"thm-2","file":"","label":"l3","number":"2.3","section":"sec-2","order":6,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{l3}\r\n Let $x,y,m,n$ be integers such that $y\u003ex\u003e1$ and $m,n\u003e1$. Then the following equation has at most one pair $(m,n)$ of solution for every fixed pair $(x,y)$:\r\n $$\\frac{y^n-1}{y-1}=\\frac{x^m-1}{x-1}.$$","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","name":"see e.g. Theorem 1.3 of","cites_in_head":["HT"],"labels":["l3"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"cited","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":102,"to":105},"hash":"sha256:b94086331a3996b758b164c8541e7c323bc70590f2a0749a48c1b094be5bc919","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-5","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"theorem","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"thm-3","file":"","label":"t1","number":"2.4","section":"sec-2","order":7,"title":"Theorem","body_md":"\\label{t1} Let $G$ be a nilpotent group with at least two distinct non-abelian Sylow subgroups. Suppose also that $H$ is any non-abelian group such that\r\n$|Z(G)|\\geq|Z(H)|$ and $\\Gamma_G\\cong\\Gamma_H$. Then $|G|=|H|$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"thm","item":"statement/theorem","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["t1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"here","origin":"own","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":107,"to":109},"hash":"sha256:f9b62e9817fd7fd932c12726f119be23226aa81669383dc9723411dff9230417","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-6","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"proof","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"proof-2","file":"","section":"sec-2","order":8,"title":"Proof","body_md":"Suppose  $G=P\\times Q\\times S$, where $P$ and $Q$ are non-abelian Sylow $p$, $q$-subgroups of $G$ such that $p\\neq q$ and\r\n $S$ is a subgroup of $G$. If\r\n$x\\in P\\setminus Z(P)$ and $y\\in Q\\setminus Z(Q)$, then\r\n$|Z(G)|\u003c |C_P(x)||C_Q(y)||S|$. Therefore\r\n$$|G||Z(G)|\u003c |C_P(x)||C_Q(y)||P||Q||S|^2=|C_G(x)||C_G(y)|.$$ It follows that\r\n $$|G||Z(G)|\u003c \\max\\{|C_G(x)|^2,|C_G(y|^2\\}.$$ Now,  Lemma \\ref{l1}(2) completes the proof.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"proof","item":"proof","head":"environment","scope":"paper","proves":"thm-3","attach":3,"span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":110,"to":116},"hash":"sha256:349c4b8195c707e9ffd938a8e41fdca46953a180d0d17c0b82d3b13e883cf7c6","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#proof-2","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
{"kind":"statement","subkind":"corollary","paper":"1304.4839","version":"1","local":"cor-1","file":"","label":"cor1","number":"2.5","section":"sec-2","order":9,"title":"Corollary","body_md":"\\label{cor1} Let $G$ and $H$ be two nilpotent groups each of which have at least two non-abelian Sylow subgroups.\r\n If $\\Gamma_G\\cong\\Gamma_H$, then $|G|=|H|$.","path":"source","confidence":"certain","env":"cor","item":"statement/corollary","head":"environment","counter":"thm","number_from":"counter","labels":["cor1"],"scope":"paper","proof_status":"cited","origin":"cited","span":{"file":"paper.tex","from":117,"to":119},"hash":"sha256:8c9c3acb2467c5e2f857eae068b744e13ca415a4b07679557fbbbf0743ebaa16","minhash":"","census":"1304.4839v1#env-7","extractor":"ax/v0.5.8"}
